{
  "table": {
    "name": "set_translations",
    "purpose": "Localized (translated) names of Magic: The Gathering sets. Grain: one row per set × language (121 sets × 10 languages = 1210 rows). This is the translations side-table of 'sets' in an MTGJSON-style database (cards, foreign_data, legalities, rulings, sets); each row gives the name of one set in one of the ten languages MTG was printed in, or null when no translation exists. Evidence: setCode values are canonical MTG set codes (10E, 4ED, TSP, M14, RTR, EVE, ARC, C16, DDR) and translation values are those sets' names in the row's language (e.g. RTR → 'Ritorno a Ravnica' in Italian)."
  },
  "columns": {
    "id": {
      "role": "identifier",
      "name": "id",
      "description": "Surrogate primary key of the translation row. Sequential integers 1–1210 (min 1, max 1210, mean 605.5, perfectly uniform quartiles), unique across all 1210 rows; carries no meaning beyond row identity.",
      "status": "resolved"
    },
    "language": {
      "role": "category",
      "name": "language",
      "description": "Language of the set-name translation. Exactly 10 distinct values, each occurring 121 times (once per set) — the languages Magic: The Gathering sets were localized into. Observed: Chinese Simplified, Chinese Traditional, French, German, Italian, Japanese, Korean, Russian; the remaining two are presumably Portuguese (Brazil) and Spanish, matching MTG's ten print languages (the sample translation 'Alvorecer' is Portuguese).",
      "status": "resolved"
    },
    "setCode": {
      "role": "foreign_key",
      "name": "set_code",
      "description": "Code of the Magic: The Gathering set whose name is translated (e.g. 10E = Tenth Edition, 4ED = Fourth Edition, TSP = Time Spiral, M14 = Magic 2014, RTR = Return to Ravnica, EVE = Eventide, ARC = Archenemy, C16 = Commander 2016, DDR = Duel Decks: Nissa vs. Ob Nixilis). Foreign key to sets.code (many-to-one, join accepted by statistics); 121 distinct codes, each appearing once per language (10 times).",
      "status": "resolved"
    },
    "translation": {
      "role": "free_text",
      "name": "translated_set_name",
      "description": "The set's name rendered in the row's language. Evidence: RTR → 'Ritorno a Ravnica' (Italian), EVE → 'イーブンタイド' (Japanese for 'Eventide'), 'Ханы Таркиры' (Russian for Khans of Tarkir), 'Базовый выпуск Magic 2015' (Russian for 'Magic 2015 Core Set'), 'Terres natales' (French for Homelands). Null in ~19% of rows (≈231) where no translation exists for that set–language pair; English set names repeated across all 10 languages (e.g. 'Ajani vs. Nicol Bolas', 'Archenemy', 'Battle Royale', 'Beatdown') mark sets whose names were not localized.",
      "status": "resolved"
    }
  }
}
